{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "chain-so2-co2e-mechanism-runspec",
    "description": "PENDING (PLAN.md 7.5 step 7d). The `chain-so2-co2e-mechanism` RunSpec -- 27 pollutant-processes over 26 pollutants, 2,767 rows. It does NOT reproduce yet. It is here because the measurement below is worth more written down than re-derived, and `n_outputRate` is bound to what THIS chain computes (1,294) rather than to what the run emits (2,767), so the document runs and says where it stops.\n\nWHAT IT WAITS ON, MEASURED 2026-09-21 rather than guessed. Every one of the 1,294 rows the chain emits is RIGHT -- 1,294 shared, 0 extra, worst cell 8.201e-06 against a 2e-05 gate. The entire gap is ABSENCE, and it is five pieces:\n\n* `SO2Calculator` -- pollutant 31, 104 rows, absent. Total Energy times a market-share-weighted sulfur level over the fuel's energy content, then `sulfateemissionrate`'s model-year group. Electricity fails it twice (no fuel-type-9 row AND a NULL `energyContent` on subtype 90) and this snapshot cannot say which one MOVES reached.\n* `CO2AERunningStartExtendedIdleCalculator` -- pollutants 90 and 98, 125 rows each, absent. Step 1a is energy x carbon x oxidation x 44/12; step 2 reads step 1a's own rows BACK and sums them with methane and N2O, each weighted by `Pollutant.globalWarmingPotential` (N2O is 265, CO2 is 1). That is a chained pollutant-process whose parents are three DIFFERENT pollutants and whose combination is an ADDITION -- the first in this chain, where every rung so far multiplies one parent by one ratio.\n* `TOGSpeciationCalculator` -- pollutant 88 NonHAPTOG, 104 rows, absent. NMOG minus the sum of one (mechanism, integratedSpeciesSet)'s members, clamped at zero. A chain rung that SUBTRACTS a set of siblings, and the only run in the corpus whose `integratedspeciesset` is non-empty: 14 rows, against 0 in every other snapshot including the misleadingly named `chain-tog-speciation`.\n* TWO MORE `AirToxicsCalculator` RATIO PATHS -- `minorHAPRatio` for the seven BTEX-family toxics 40 to 46 (728 rows) and `pahGasRatio` for naphthalene gas 185 (104 rows), both absent. `minorhapratio` is 2,697 national rows keyed by (pollutant-process, fuel TYPE, fuel SUBTYPE, model-year group) and `pahgasratio` is 452 keyed without the subtype -- a fourth and a fifth keying of the same idea, beside `atratio`'s formulation and `atrationongas`'s (subtype, source type).\n* THREE TOXICS THIS CHAIN ALREADY HALF-EMITS -- ethanol 21 (3 of 64), acetaldehyde 26 and acrolein 27 (43 of 104 each). Their non-gasoline half already works, through the `ATRatioNonGas` path this chain ports; what is missing is the gasoline half, which is `generalFuelRatioExpression` rows and Complex Model configurations for pollutant-processes 2101, 2601 and 2701. That is DATA in the two relations `runspecs/process-airtoxics.esm` already added -- `atx_*` and the air-toxics configurations -- and not new machinery.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT WAIT ON, which is the useful half of the measurement. The second rate root is already here: Total Energy (pollutant 91, 125 rows) and N2O (pollutant 6, 124 rows) come off the age-INDEPENDENT `emissionrate` where THC comes off `emissionratebyage`, and both reproduce exactly. So do THC, methane, NMHC, NMOG, TOG, VOC, benzene, 1,3-butadiene and formaldehyde. Eleven of the twenty-six pollutants are complete before a line of this rung is written, and the CO2 the two calculators above need is a multiple of a number this chain already has right.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "chain-tog-speciation",
      "hc-speciation",
      "chained",
      "ragged",
      "fixed-point"
    ]
  },
